    "Core 2.5.7 and Interface 1.9.1 source tests are backed by byte-for-byte comparison of their 22 runtime / 17 source JavaScript files in actual npm tarballs. Rebuilt interface distribution files differ from the published bundles, so source equivalence is not a claim of byte-identical builds. Published adapter checks exercise actual registry peers separately.",
    "Core 2.5.7 fixes recurrence DST drift, but historical full-suite failures under Los Angeles/Kolkata remain documented from the 2 October release candidate. The unchanged release passes the fresh UTC suite and 696-fixture recurrence matrix. No fresh full cross-host run or blanket timezone-correctness claim is made.",
    "jsdom integration and SSR tests are not real-browser, Salesforce, CSP or independent penetration tests.",
    "Direct interface root import needs a DOM; bare-Node direct import raises HTMLElement is not defined. Adapters remain SSR-safe in the existing tests through lazy client import. Do not describe all package-root imports as bare-Node/SSR-safe.",
    "Core and interface packages do not export a package.json subpath. Version checks for them read the installed manifest; package.json subpath checks apply only to React/Vue adapters.",
